WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.916 --> 00:00:41.208
<b>Lord Shri Krishna now begins to answer </b>
<b>Arjuna's question.</b>

2
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:42.791
<b>He tells Arjuna</b>

3
00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:49.458
<b>that so far, he has described two paths </b>
<b>for spiritual attainment in this world</b>

4
00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:53.833
<b>- one is the path of knowledge (Gnana Yoga) </b>
<b>associated with the Sankhya philosophy,</b>

5
00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:57.500
<b>and the other is the path of selfless action</b>
<b>(Nishkaam Karma Yoga).</b>

6
00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:03.875
<b>In the second chapter,</b>

7
00:01:03.875 --> 00:01:07.458
<b>Shri Krishna explained two types of people</b>

8
00:01:07.458 --> 00:01:14.958
<b>and the appropriate paths </b>
<b>of spiritual attainment for both:</b>

9
00:01:14.958 --> 00:01:16.583
<b>First are those</b>

10
00:01:16.583 --> 00:01:23.541
<b>who completely renounce action and adopt the </b>
<b>path of inner contemplation and knowledge.</b>

11
00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:27.958
<b>They achieve spiritual attainment </b>
<b>through this medium.</b>

12
00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:30.875
<b>In the verse 49 of the second chapter,</b>

13
00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:35.250
<b>this philosophy, known </b>
<b>as Sankhya, was mentioned.</b>

14
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.166
<b>According to this school of thought,</b>

15
00:01:37.166 --> 00:01:43.833
<b>one can know and attain their spiritual </b>
<b>truth through critical study.</b>

16
00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:45.875
<b>Second are those,</b>

17
00:01:45.875 --> 00:01:51.791
<b>who have a greater inclination towards </b>
<b>action than study and inner contemplation.</b>

18
00:01:51.791 --> 00:01:57.625
<b>They can also achieve spiritual attainment </b>
<b>through only action.</b>

19
00:01:57.625 --> 00:02:02.500
<b>This spiritual path is called selfless</b>
<b>(Nishkaam) Karma Yoga,</b>

20
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:08.708
<b>where a person performs his duties </b>
<b>selflessly while living in this world,</b>

21
00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:13.125
<b>but without attachment to </b>
<b>the results of their actions.</b>

22
00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:17.041
<b>They renounce all desires for</b>
<b>the fruits of their work.</b>

23
00:02:17.041 --> 00:02:22.250
<b>One is a Gnana Yogi, while </b>
<b>the other is a Karma Yogi.</b>

24
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.125
<b>Though the paths are different,</b>

25
00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:27.375
<b>their purpose is the same:</b>

26
00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:32.125
<b>to know the spiritual truth and</b>
<b>unite with the Supreme.</b>

27
00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:35.166
<b>Arjuna is confused between these two,</b>

28
00:02:35.166 --> 00:02:37.958
<b>perhaps thinking</b>

29
00:02:37.958 --> 00:02:41.041
<b>that the destinations of these paths are different,</b>

30
00:02:41.041 --> 00:02:44.291
<b>or that one path is better than the other.</b>

31
00:02:44.291 --> 00:02:45.875
<b>Due to this confusion,</b>

32
00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:52.541
<b>he had requested Krishna in the previous </b>
<b>verses to suggest a definite path.</b>

33
00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:54.625
<b>Think about it.</b>

34
00:02:58.958 --> 00:03:01.458
<b>A life</b>

35
00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:06.791
<b>without any accountability to anyone,</b>

36
00:03:06.791 --> 00:03:11.541
<b>and no responsibilities on one's shoulders.</b>

37
00:03:11.541 --> 00:03:12.875
<b>If there's anything,</b>

38
00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:18.958
<b>it's just the comfort.</b>

39
00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:21.541
<b>If given such an option,</b>

40
00:03:21.541 --> 00:03:25.333
<b>a person would choose it immediately. </b>

41
00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:29.083
<b>After all, where else would one find a happier life?</b>

42
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:33.583
<b>And this is the biggest misconception,</b>

43
00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:39.958
<b>that a life without duty </b>
<b>and only comfort is a happy life.</b>

44
00:03:39.958 --> 00:03:42.250
<b>If this were true,</b>

45
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:49.416
<b>then anyone with an abundance of </b>
<b>wealth, resources, and comforts</b>

46
00:03:49.416 --> 00:03:52.500
<b>would always be happy.</b>

47
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.875
<b>But that's not the case.</b>

48
00:03:55.875 --> 00:03:59.666
<b>You know this too.</b>

49
00:03:59.666 --> 00:04:00.791
<b>So why</b>

50
00:04:00.791 --> 00:04:04.833
<b>does one live with this notion?</b>

51
00:04:04.833 --> 00:04:05.958
<b>Why</b>

52
00:04:05.958 --> 00:04:10.833
<b>seek happiness in worldly objects?</b>

53
00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:13.750
<b>Happiness and joy</b>

54
00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:19.375
<b>depends on a person's heart and state of mind,</b>

55
00:04:19.375 --> 00:04:22.208
<b>not on external things.</b>

56
00:04:22.208 --> 00:04:25.458
<b>If a person's mind is pure,</b>

57
00:04:25.458 --> 00:04:28.541
<b>they will experience happiness,</b>

58
00:04:28.541 --> 00:04:33.041
<b>regardless of external circumstances.</b>

59
00:04:33.041 --> 00:04:35.708
<b>Conversely,</b>

60
00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:40.666
<b>even if the external situation </b>
<b>is extremely comfortable,</b>

61
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:44.125
<b>if the mind is not pure and peaceful,</b>

62
00:04:44.125 --> 00:04:49.250
<b>it's impossible to experience happiness.</b>

63
00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.166
<b>Think about it.</b>

64
00:04:51.166 --> 00:04:56.916
<b>Consider a situation where </b>
<b>you perform your duties,</b>

65
00:04:56.916 --> 00:04:59.208
<b>but your mind is so pure</b>

66
00:04:59.208 --> 00:05:06.166
<b>that it has no desires, no distortions.</b>

67
00:05:06.166 --> 00:05:10.208
<b>How satisfying this state would be.</b>

68
00:05:10.208 --> 00:05:13.333
<b>How peaceful.</b>

69
00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:17.375
<b>This is the attainment of true happiness.</b>

70
00:05:17.375 --> 00:05:19.541
<b>Strive to focus</b>

71
00:05:19.541 --> 00:05:26.166
<b>solely on your actions like a yogi,</b>

72
00:05:26.166 --> 00:05:28.583
<b>that's what's in your hands.</b>

73
00:05:28.583 --> 00:05:37.750
<b>And why be disturbed by thoughts of </b>
<b>results that are not in your control?</b>

74
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.250
<b>This mindset</b>

75
00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:43.333
<b>will lead you towards happiness.</b>

76
00:05:47.625 --> 00:05:49.833
<b>Whether it's the path of knowledge</b>

77
00:05:49.833 --> 00:05:50.916
<b>or</b>

78
00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:54.750
<b>selfless action,</b>

79
00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:59.583
<b>both lead to happiness and spirituality.</b>

80
00:05:59.583 --> 00:06:03.791
<b>These are just two different paths</b>

81
00:06:03.791 --> 00:06:08.250
<b>with the same destination.</b>

82
00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:15.666
<b>Here, comparisons of right/wrong </b>
<b>or better/worse should not be made.</b>

83
00:06:15.666 --> 00:06:16.958
<b>Similarly,</b>

84
00:06:16.958 --> 00:06:21.375
<b>in a family, the elders should understand </b>

85
00:06:21.375 --> 00:06:33.166
<b>that constantly comparing between </b>
<b>younger ones or between two children is wrong. </b>

86
00:06:33.166 --> 00:06:35.625
<b>Everyone has a different level,</b>

87
00:06:35.625 --> 00:06:38.208
<b>their abilities are different,</b>

88
00:06:38.208 --> 00:06:43.666
<b>no one is completely good or bad.</b>

89
00:06:43.666 --> 00:06:45.250
<b>But</b>

90
00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.916
<b>this comparison is often made,</b>

91
00:06:48.916 --> 00:06:54.166
<b>which can have a negative impact.</b>

92
00:06:54.166 --> 00:06:58.083
<b>A person who is constantly criticized</b>

93
00:06:58.083 --> 00:07:03.500
<b>either loses self-confidence </b>

94
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.625
<b>or,</b>

95
00:07:04.625 --> 00:07:06.791
<b>contrary to this,</b>

96
00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:12.375
<b>may choose the path of rebellion </b>
<b>and go down the wrong path.</b>

97
00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:17.500
<b>Neither of these situations is good.</b>

98
00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.541
<b>It's the responsibility of parents</b>

99
00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:27.500
<b>to maintain a positive atmosphere in the family.</b>

100
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:32.041
<b>Instead of comparing good/bad among </b>
<b>the younger ones,</b>

101
00:07:32.041 --> 00:07:38.708
<b>they should highlight their good qualities, </b>
<b>boost their confidence,</b>

102
00:07:38.708 --> 00:07:43.458
<b>and inspire them to become better.</b>

103
00:07:43.458 --> 00:07:48.833
<b>And part of this process of becoming better,</b>

104
00:07:48.833 --> 00:07:51.583
<b>is internal improvement.</b>

105
00:07:51.583 --> 00:07:53.041
<b>Try to ensure</b>

106
00:07:53.041 --> 00:07:56.666
<b>that you and your family</b>

107
00:07:56.666 --> 00:08:00.083
<b>move towards this internal improvement.</b>

108
00:08:00.083 --> 00:08:03.083
<b>Along with worldly goals,</b>

109
00:08:03.083 --> 00:08:06.416
<b>it's necessary to understand the </b>
<b>importance of human relationships, mutual love,</b>

110
00:08:06.416 --> 00:08:13.041
<b>and proper life values. </b>
<b>It's important to follow them.</b>

111
00:08:13.041 --> 00:08:24.791
<b>And as an elder in the family, </b>
<b>this is your responsibility.</b>

112
00:08:28.958 --> 00:08:33.541
<b>Two different paths leading to spirituality,</b>

113
00:08:33.541 --> 00:08:36.458
<b>two different perspectives –</b>

114
00:08:36.458 --> 00:08:38.833
<b>one of knowledge yoga,</b>

115
00:08:38.833 --> 00:08:41.083
<b>one of karma yoga.</b>

116
00:08:41.083 --> 00:08:43.083
<b>In professional life too,</b>

117
00:08:43.083 --> 00:08:48.625
<b>diversity of perspectives is common.</b>

118
00:08:48.625 --> 00:08:55.875
<b>Each and everyone tries </b>
<b>to solve problems in their own way.</b>

119
00:08:55.875 --> 00:08:58.583
<b>Where, some people stop,</b>

120
00:08:58.583 --> 00:09:00.291
<b>think,</b>

121
00:09:00.291 --> 00:09:02.333
<b>and then decide,</b>

122
00:09:02.333 --> 00:09:07.000
<b>while others believe in immediate action.</b>

123
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.083
<b>Some, without reaching the root of the problem</b>

124
00:09:10.083 --> 00:09:15.666
<b>and fully understanding it </b>
<b>won't take the next step.</b>

125
00:09:15.666 --> 00:09:17.666
<b>while others</b>

126
00:09:17.666 --> 00:09:27.666
<b>start doing their work first to</b>
<b>save time and then improve later.</b>

127
00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:29.750
<b>Both these methods</b>

128
00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.458
<b>are appropriate in different situations.</b>

129
00:09:33.458 --> 00:09:35.458
<b>And in professional life,</b>

130
00:09:35.458 --> 00:09:39.000
<b>you'll find colleagues of both types.</b>

131
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.833
<b>Depending on the situation,</b>

132
00:09:40.833 --> 00:09:47.000
<b>it's up to you to decide who to assign what work.</b>

133
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.875
<b>Both have their place.</b>

134
00:09:49.875 --> 00:09:54.958
<b>Both are capable in their own ways.</b>

